# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored — never commit real values) for
# local frontend development against a running backend. See
# docs/reference-environment.md for how to bring up that backend
# (docker compose) and its own .env.example at the repository root for
# API_TOKEN.
#
# Scope: like the root .env.example, this is local development
# configuration only — not a production secrets-delivery mechanism. This
# repository does not yet define a production frontend deployment. See
# "Production boundary" below for the intended real architecture.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two different kinds of variable live in this file. Do not confuse them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# VITE_* variables are PUBLIC. Vite inlines every `VITE_`-prefixed
# variable into the built client bundle — anyone who loads the page can
# read it in plain text (view-source, devtools, the built JS files on
# disk). Nothing secret may ever be given a `VITE_` prefix. This project
# currently defines no `VITE_*` variable at all, specifically because a
# bearer credential must never be one.
#
# API_PROXY_TOKEN (below) is SERVER-SIDE development-proxy configuration.
# It has no `VITE_` prefix on purpose, is read only by vite.config.ts
# (Node.js, via `loadEnv`), and is never bundled into client code or
# reachable from the browser. It must never be renamed to start with
# `VITE_`.

# Node-side only (read by vite.config.ts via loadEnv, never bundled into
# client code): where the dev/preview server's /api/* proxy forwards
# requests. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8080, matching
# docker-compose.yml's default APP_PORT -- override only if your backend
# is reachable somewhere else (a different APP_PORT, a remote host).
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# Node-side only, server-side credential: must match the backend's own
# API_TOKEN (root .env.example) exactly. The dev/preview proxy attaches
# this as the Authorization header on every proxied /api/* request,
# after it has already left the browser — the browser itself never
# constructs, holds, or sends this value. Required: `npm run dev` and
# `npm run preview` (and therefore `npm run e2e`) refuse to start their
# /api proxy without it.
API_PROXY_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production boundary (not implemented by this local proxy)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This developer proxy is a local convenience, not a production
# authentication architecture. It exists only so `npm run dev`/`preview`
# can reach a real backend without the browser needing a credential or
# the Go backend needing a CORS policy. It does not model, and must not
# be mistaken for, how this product would authenticate real users in
# production. The intended production model is:
#
#   - the browser and the frontend are served from one public origin;
#   - `/api/*` under that same origin is handled by a production reverse
#     proxy or backend-for-frontend (BFF), not this Vite dev server;
#   - browser-facing authentication uses a real user/session boundary
#     (e.g. a session cookie issued by that BFF after login) — never a
#     shared bearer token typed into browser-reachable configuration;
#   - the shared service credential this file's API_PROXY_TOKEN stands
#     in for stays server-side always, held by the reverse proxy/BFF,
#     never the browser;
#   - TLS terminates in front of that public origin;
#   - the Go API itself is not directly exposed to an arbitrary browser
#     origin.
#
# None of that production architecture is built yet — it is a
# deliberately deferred decision (ARCH-01 §9), not something this local
# proxy attempts to approximate.
